                      (    forth6809.asm):05403                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):05404                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):05405                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):05406                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):05407                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):05408                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
                      (    forth6809.asm):05409                                  ; "-123 S>D" returned high cell 0 instead of
                      (    forth6809.asm):05410                                  ; -1 - no sign extension was happening at all.
